WEBVTT

00:04.504 --> 00:07.337
Thanks for baby-sitting, Meg.
We'll be back in a couple of hours.

00:07.440 --> 00:09.908
I don't understand why
I have to baby-sit Stewie.

00:10.010 --> 00:12.706
I mean, what's he really gonna do
if we leave him by himself?

00:12.812 --> 00:15.440
And now to test my teleportation pods.

00:18.618 --> 00:19.846
Oh, damn!

00:24.758 --> 00:26.885
I'm a monster!

00:27.494 --> 00:30.895
<i>[Singing] It seems today that all you see</i>

00:30.997 --> 00:34.160
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:34.267 --> 00:37.668
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:37.771 --> 00:40.535
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:40.940 --> 00:43.636
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:44.277 --> 00:47.474
<i>Lucky there's a man who
Positively can do</i>

00:47.580 --> 00:49.104
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:49.215 --> 00:50.443
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:50.984 --> 00:55.819
<i>He's a family guy</i>

01:02.929 --> 01:06.695
So, this is awkward, but...

01:06.900 --> 01:10.301
have we ever actually, you know, met?

01:10.737 --> 01:15.003
I mean, you know, I don't even know, say,
for example, if you have a room up there.

01:15.375 --> 01:17.240
You know, a room?

01:17.811 --> 01:19.142
I have a room.

01:20.647 --> 01:22.342
You know, Meg, if you kill yourself now...

01:22.449 --> 01:24.849
you'll probably get a full page
in the yearbook.

01:24.951 --> 01:27.715
So, you know,
that's something to think about.

01:28.088 --> 01:29.282
Just burped.

01:29.389 --> 01:30.413
[Doorbell rings]

01:30.523 --> 01:31.490
Hi, Meg.

01:31.591 --> 01:33.491
You busy Saturday night?

01:33.593 --> 01:37.120
Neil, you ask me out, like, once a day,
and I always give you the same answer.

01:37.230 --> 01:38.219
No!

01:38.331 --> 01:42.062
God, I don't think I could have been any
clearer the last time I turned him down.

01:42.168 --> 01:45.194
<i>Ray, your mother insulted
my steak pizzola again.</i>

01:45.705 --> 01:48.139
<i>Neil Goldman of Quahog, Rhode Island...</i>

01:48.241 --> 01:49.936
<i>leave me alone!</i>

01:50.043 --> 01:52.443
<i>I hate you! I hate you!</i>

01:53.213 --> 01:56.205
<i>- Anyway, your mother insulted...
- I don't care anymore, Patty.</i>

01:56.316 --> 01:58.716
<i>After nine seasons, I just don't care.</i>

01:58.818 --> 02:01.412
<i>Maybe you could try not being a bitch.</i>

02:03.256 --> 02:04.951
[Jazzy instrumental music]

02:08.928 --> 02:10.953
Hey, Mort.
Lois and I are out on our date night.

02:11.064 --> 02:12.463
Why don't you give me some condoms?

02:12.565 --> 02:16.558
And some Excedrin.
My wife's got a headache this big.

02:16.870 --> 02:18.861
You know, it's like from the commercial.

02:18.972 --> 02:21.270
This big. Only it's my junk.

02:21.374 --> 02:24.138
All right, then. $12.43.

02:24.244 --> 02:27.179
Jeez, that's more of a rip-off
than that breakfast machine I bought.

02:51.471 --> 02:53.530
Ow! Ow!

02:53.640 --> 02:55.574
What was the point of all that?

02:56.743 --> 03:00.611
All it does is shoot you.
It doesn't make breakfast at all.

03:01.748 --> 03:03.079
Besides, I forgot my wallet.

03:03.183 --> 03:05.048
Well, that's okay. I'll just open up a tab.

03:05.151 --> 03:08.211
Wait a minute, what the hell's a tab?
Does that mean I don't gotta pay?

03:08.321 --> 03:10.346
- Well, not right now, but...
- Ah, sweet!

03:10.456 --> 03:12.981
<i>Hey, while I'm at it,
give me all these copies of Marie Claire.</i>

03:13.092 --> 03:15.026
You know, in case I want to
rub out that easy one...

03:15.128 --> 03:16.459
before I get Lois into bed tonight.

03:16.563 --> 03:18.827
Kathleen Turner's on Page 45.

03:18.932 --> 03:21.730
Kathleen Turner, huh?
Let's see how she looks.

03:21.834 --> 03:23.096
Oh, that's a shame.

03:25.004 --> 03:27.370
<i>COMMENTATOR: [On TV] And now back to
The Kids' Choice Awards...</i>

03:27.473 --> 03:29.270
<i>with host Paula Poundstone.</i>

03:29.375 --> 03:32.071
<i>I choose you and you and you.</i>

03:32.312 --> 03:33.404
<i>So, come on.</i>

03:34.681 --> 03:36.171
<i>I said, let's go!</i>

03:36.516 --> 03:38.575
[Children whimpering]

03:40.820 --> 03:42.048
STEWIE: Meg!

03:42.322 --> 03:44.313
Meg, I'm hungry!

03:44.657 --> 03:48.218
There's a granola bar in the cupboard.
I want it.

03:49.729 --> 03:50.718
Hey.

03:51.030 --> 03:52.019
Hey.

03:52.332 --> 03:53.356
What's this?

03:53.766 --> 03:54.858
What's going on?

03:55.134 --> 03:56.396
Am I talking to myself up there?

03:56.502 --> 03:59.528
Oh, my God.
Stewie, just shut up and go to bed!

03:59.639 --> 04:03.166
Do you know what I do, Meg?
I spit in your mouth while you sleep.

04:03.943 --> 04:08.073
Finally. Look, Mom, I've had it.
I am not baby-sitting anymore.

04:08.181 --> 04:10.547
It's Saturday night,
I could be out having a life.

04:10.650 --> 04:13.141
Meg, if you don't want
to baby-sit anymore, that's fine.

04:13.253 --> 04:15.483
But don't you stand there and lie to me.

04:15.588 --> 04:19.456
Meg, she torched your ass, man.
She torched your ass.

04:19.559 --> 04:21.891
Why can't you just hire a real baby-sitter?

04:21.995 --> 04:23.519
Well, I guess we could do that.

04:23.630 --> 04:25.757
Damn! I'm terrible at meeting new people.

04:25.865 --> 04:27.492
<i>Like the time I was on Blind Date.</i>

04:27.967 --> 04:30.265
- I'm having a great time, Stewie.
- Me, too.

04:30.370 --> 04:32.930
So, you ready to go grab some 'za?

04:33.740 --> 04:34.764
Yeah.

04:40.079 --> 04:41.410
So, a wild guess here...

04:41.514 --> 04:44.244
but from the looks of your arm hair,
I'm guessing you're Italian?

04:49.889 --> 04:53.689
All right, you guys, I got eight crates
of ipecac from Mort, all on my tab.

04:53.793 --> 04:55.658
Now, whoever goes the longest
without puking...

04:55.762 --> 04:57.957
gets the last piece of pie in the fridge.

04:59.766 --> 05:01.427
Okay, here we go.

05:03.169 --> 05:05.694
- How's everybody doing?
- Good. Good so far.

05:05.805 --> 05:07.102
All right, all right.

05:07.206 --> 05:09.003
- Nothing yet.
- Cool, cool.

05:09.442 --> 05:12.900
You know, I don't know if you guys
had any of that pie already...

05:13.246 --> 05:17.307
but that is some tasty stuff.
That's from the bake sale that Lois...

05:18.551 --> 05:21.850
One down. I know somebody
who won't be having any...

05:22.789 --> 05:24.586
I'm starting to feel funny.

05:24.857 --> 05:26.916
Well, I feel fine. I guess I'm...

05:27.760 --> 05:31.252
Oh, boy! That means I win. I get to eat...

05:34.267 --> 05:36.929
Oh, God! Why didn't anybody tell me...

05:38.571 --> 05:41.039
Oh, my God! My insides are on...

05:42.375 --> 05:45.037
No. No, please. No more, no more. No...

05:46.245 --> 05:48.475
Dad, I'm scared.

05:49.882 --> 05:51.747
Get the phone. Call 911...

05:52.919 --> 05:55.319
Lois! Lois! Lois, get in here...

05:56.956 --> 06:00.255
Okay, okay. I think it's all gone.

06:00.893 --> 06:02.224
I think...

06:02.729 --> 06:05.027
I don't wanna, I don't wanna...

06:05.965 --> 06:08.456
Peter. Peter, I need you to hold my ears...

06:17.110 --> 06:18.338
Who wants chowder?

06:23.383 --> 06:24.611
What the hell?

06:24.717 --> 06:26.412
Hey, Meg, you better check this out.

06:26.552 --> 06:27.746
[Airplane roaring]

06:47.640 --> 06:51.872
Oh, God, this is so embarrassing.
I can't believe this is happening to me.

06:51.978 --> 06:55.277
Looks like someone could use
a greeting card to cheer them up.

06:55.381 --> 06:57.872
<i>I put these on my tab.
Here, take a Far Side one.</i>

06:57.984 --> 06:59.952
The vulture thinks he's a cowboy.

07:01.621 --> 07:02.781
It's kind of funny.

07:02.889 --> 07:06.381
Hey, Peter, you got a card for
if you transferred VD to somebody?

07:06.492 --> 07:07.959
Let's see here.

07:08.161 --> 07:10.925
Yup. "Sorry I accidentally gave you VD."

07:11.030 --> 07:13.863
That's all you got is accidental, huh?
All right, I'll take it.

07:13.966 --> 07:16.730
Well, first let me thank you
for answering the ad.

07:16.836 --> 07:21.205
Now, what do you feel qualifies you
to be an effective baby-sitter for Stewie?

07:21.307 --> 07:22.501
[Speaking in Portuguese]

07:24.510 --> 07:29.209
Yeah. We couldn't run an ad
that said "no Portuguese," but...

07:30.583 --> 07:32.312
no Portuguese.

07:34.120 --> 07:37.578
So, I see here you worked for a family
for a number of years.

07:37.690 --> 07:40.557
Can I call the Herculoids for a reference?

07:40.726 --> 07:41.988
[Babbling]

07:42.094 --> 07:43.789
I'm sorry, I don't understand.

07:45.364 --> 07:46.991
The position has been filled.

07:48.367 --> 07:51.825
The position has been filled.
Thank you very much. You can go now.

07:51.971 --> 07:53.871
[Babbling angrily]

07:55.842 --> 07:57.139
Leave! Now!

07:58.010 --> 08:00.774
I didn't think it was gonna be this hard
to choose a baby-sitter.

08:00.880 --> 08:02.472
Yes, if only you were this discerning...

08:02.582 --> 08:05.278
when you picked that happening
Bruce Jenner hairdo.

08:05.685 --> 08:08.017
Sorry I'm late. Can I still apply for the job?

08:08.221 --> 08:09.984
[Romantic instrumental music]

08:14.393 --> 08:18.557
<i>My God, I haven't been this exhilarated
since Brian took me to see Les Miserables.</i>

08:18.831 --> 08:20.321
<i>HOST: Attention, ladies and gentlemen.</i>

08:20.433 --> 08:22.458
<i>There will be a slight change
in the cast tonight.</i>

08:22.568 --> 08:23.557
Oh, no.

08:23.669 --> 08:24.966
<i>For this evening's performance...</i>

08:25.071 --> 08:28.529
<i>the role of Jean Valjean
will be played by Kirk Cameron.</i>

08:28.674 --> 08:30.164
Oh! Oh!

08:30.309 --> 08:34.336
Unbelievable! Oh, my God!
How lucky are we, huh?

08:34.447 --> 08:36.108
"Hey, Stewie,
what are you doing tonight?"

08:36.215 --> 08:39.241
"Oh, nothing. Just watching
Kirk Cameron play Jean Valjean."

08:39.352 --> 08:41.411
Oh, my God! Curtain up.

08:44.257 --> 08:46.691
Hey, Mort, do these suppositories
come in other flavors?

08:46.792 --> 08:48.191
Peter, are you eating those?

08:48.294 --> 08:49.625
No, I'm shoving them up my butt.

08:49.729 --> 08:51.321
Of course I'm eating them.
Give me a carton.

08:51.430 --> 08:54.297
Peter, it's the end of the month,
and I'm calling your tab.

08:54.400 --> 08:57.699
- You owe me $34,000.
- What?

08:57.803 --> 09:00.271
Oh, man, how am I gonna come up
with that kind of money?

09:00.373 --> 09:02.364
Peter, I'm waiting.

09:05.811 --> 09:07.711
All right, all right.
Listen, I got another idea.

09:07.813 --> 09:09.405
What if I sold you my daughter?

09:09.949 --> 09:12.474
You drop the tab,
and your son can have Meg.

09:12.818 --> 09:13.807
MEG: What?

09:13.920 --> 09:15.751
Yep, all you gotta do is sign this contract.

09:15.855 --> 09:19.552
Are you out of your mind?
You can't sell me, you fat son of a bitch!

09:19.659 --> 09:22.093
Whoa! Careful getting this fish
off the hook, Mort.

09:22.194 --> 09:23.786
She's got some fangs.

09:24.564 --> 09:27.362
What do you think of that, Neil?
Daddy bought you a girlfriend.

09:27.466 --> 09:31.334
Excuse me. If anybody is interested,
I already have a girlfriend.

09:31.437 --> 09:33.268
There's no way... Wait, what?

09:33.372 --> 09:34.600
You ready to go, honey?

09:34.707 --> 09:37.972
You rejected me too many times, Meg.
I couldn't wait for you forever.

09:38.077 --> 09:41.706
Besides, Cecilia thinks
my psoriasis is sexy.

09:42.114 --> 09:43.547
I can't believe he's over me.

09:43.649 --> 09:45.981
I can't believe I'm out $34,000.

09:46.085 --> 09:48.076
I can't believe it's not butter.

09:48.554 --> 09:50.545
<i>Stick around. More Family Guy coming up.</i>

09:55.561 --> 09:58.291
Peter, how could you have tried
to sell our daughter?

09:58.397 --> 10:02.493
All right, Lois, I don't want this to ruin
our date night, so I'll make it up to you.

10:02.902 --> 10:04.335
Oh, Peter.

10:04.470 --> 10:07.030
"I'm sorry I tried to sell our daughter."

10:07.139 --> 10:10.006
Yeah, you don't know how hard it was
to find one of those in English.

10:11.110 --> 10:13.578
Tonight the baby-sitter comes, Rupert.

10:13.679 --> 10:14.976
Lovely LaDawn.

10:18.451 --> 10:21.215
Hey, LaDawn. Hey, what's going on?
How are you?

10:21.420 --> 10:23.115
Yeah. Just me, Stewie.

10:23.389 --> 10:25.050
Just being myself.

10:26.125 --> 10:28.821
Yeah. Well, this here? It's just my package.

10:30.796 --> 10:33.629
Just my package.
God delivered it, I signed for it.

10:33.733 --> 10:36.463
World keeps on spinning. Yeah.

10:38.437 --> 10:39.597
Oh, no!

10:40.039 --> 10:41.768
Jenga, there it is.

10:43.042 --> 10:45.374
Well, I guess that's why they call it Jenga.

10:46.245 --> 10:48.907
Stewie, you're so cute,
I can't even stand it.

10:49.015 --> 10:51.245
Thank you. I'm having a good time, too.

10:51.350 --> 10:53.318
<i>I hope I don't make any social faux pas...</i>

10:53.419 --> 10:56.252
like I did at Pamela and Tommy Lee's
dinner party.

10:56.355 --> 10:58.983
Hi, sorry I'm late.
I was visiting my aunt in the hospital.

10:59.091 --> 11:02.720
She has hepatitis.

11:05.698 --> 11:06.926
Sorry.

11:12.038 --> 11:14.029
CECILIA: Neil is such an amazing guy.

11:14.140 --> 11:16.506
We just make
an absolutely perfect couple.

11:16.609 --> 11:18.509
You know, Neil liked me first.

11:18.611 --> 11:21.910
And I was gonna go out with him
when I was ready to settle for him.

11:22.014 --> 11:23.447
Get your own spaz.

11:24.183 --> 11:25.980
All right, ladies, enough chitchat.

11:26.085 --> 11:28.747
Take it off, get in the shower
and bounce around for me.

11:31.257 --> 11:33.782
Sweetie, your daddy and I
are going to the movies tonight.

11:33.893 --> 11:35.588
How would you like LaDawn to baby-sit?

11:35.695 --> 11:38.528
Yes! I'm going to wow her tonight, Rupert.

11:38.631 --> 11:41.532
I'm gonna be cooler than Brian
when he hangs out at the bowling alley.

11:41.701 --> 11:44.261
That's what I love about high-school girls.

11:44.370 --> 11:47.271
I keep getting older,
they stay the same age.

11:48.007 --> 11:50.737
Yes, they do. Yes, they do.

11:53.079 --> 11:55.980
Please go out with me.
I'm just trying to make Neil jealous.

11:56.082 --> 11:57.811
I promise, I'll pay and everything.

11:57.917 --> 12:01.717
Yeah. That sounds cool,
but I'm gonna be in the hospital that night.

12:09.361 --> 12:11.158
[Screaming in pain]

12:15.601 --> 12:18.661
- Hi, gorgeous man.
- Oh, you.

12:18.771 --> 12:22.172
Must I lock up your tongue
with the rest of the silver?

12:22.408 --> 12:24.706
Stewie, this is Jeremy.

12:24.810 --> 12:28.371
Hey, little man. So you're the guy
who's been trying to steal my girlfriend.

12:28.481 --> 12:29.573
What... You...

12:29.715 --> 12:30.943
Girlfriend?

12:31.050 --> 12:33.484
What kind of sick, twisted game
are you playing at?

12:33.586 --> 12:36.384
Stewie sounds a little cranky.
I'll put him to bed.

12:36.522 --> 12:39.047
I got your hat! Take that, hatless!

12:39.225 --> 12:42.353
Now go back to the quad
and resume your Hacky Sack tourney!

12:42.461 --> 12:44.827
I'm not gonna lie down
for some frat-boy bastard...

12:44.930 --> 12:47.421
with his damn Teva sandals
and his Skoal Bandits...

12:47.533 --> 12:50.297
and his Abercrombie & Fitch
long-sleeved, open-stitched...

12:50.402 --> 12:53.235
crew-neck Henley smoking his sticky buds
out of a soda can...

12:53.339 --> 12:56.536
<i>while watching his favorite downloaded
Simpsons episodes every night!</i>

12:56.642 --> 13:00.009
Yes, we all love Mr. Plow.
You've got the song memorized, do you?

13:00.112 --> 13:01.306
So does everyone else!

13:01.413 --> 13:04.940
That is exactly the kind of idiot you see
at Taco Bell at 1:00 in the morning.

13:05.050 --> 13:07.780
The guy who just whiffed his way
down the bar-skank ladder.

13:07.887 --> 13:09.149
Good night, Stewie.

13:09.255 --> 13:11.314
If he wants to throw hands,
I'll throw hands.

13:11.423 --> 13:12.913
I tell you...

13:21.333 --> 13:23.893
Hey! Neil and Cecilia.

13:24.036 --> 13:25.560
I didn't expect to see you here.

13:25.704 --> 13:27.535
Meet Jake, my boyfriend.

13:27.640 --> 13:30.507
I want some BB's.
My dad lets me shoot at cats.

13:30.609 --> 13:31.667
Hi, Meg.

13:31.877 --> 13:34.937
Neil and I are celebrating
our two-week anniversary.

13:35.047 --> 13:36.605
It seems like only yesterday...

13:36.715 --> 13:39.513
he was just a stranger
videotaping me through the window.

13:39.618 --> 13:42.212
Big deal.
He did that to me three years ago.

13:42.321 --> 13:44.312
And he gave me the tapes for Christmas.

13:44.423 --> 13:45.913
He gave me DVDs.

13:46.025 --> 13:49.893
<i>The production values were amazing,
much better than Kramer vs. Predator.</i>

13:49.995 --> 13:50.962
You want him back?

13:51.063 --> 13:53.827
You can't just disappear for three months
and then suddenly decide...

13:53.933 --> 13:56.094
you want him back! You can't have him!

13:59.872 --> 14:02.033
Well, I'm glad Neil's over me, anyway.

14:02.141 --> 14:04.132
I'm with Jake now. Right, Jake?

14:04.243 --> 14:07.269
Maybe someday we'll get married
and you can go up on me.

14:07.780 --> 14:10.078
- Neil, I wanna be your girlfriend.
- What?

14:10.182 --> 14:13.447
I was wrong to drive you away.
We belong together.

14:13.552 --> 14:17.511
Of course, I'm understandably skeptical
of your newfound affection for me.

14:17.623 --> 14:20.023
You still got that contract
our dads drew up?

14:20.426 --> 14:21.654
Give me that.

14:25.664 --> 14:27.723
- You wanna hook up?
- Buy me something.

14:33.005 --> 14:36.372
I can't believe we're going out.
This is so cool.

14:38.177 --> 14:40.145
Neil. Neil, not so fast.

14:40.813 --> 14:44.010
Meg, you need to fulfill
your contractual obligations.

14:44.116 --> 14:45.606
What are you talking about?

14:47.319 --> 14:49.583
All right, Meg, according to the contract...

14:49.688 --> 14:51.918
every night,
you have to put on my pajamas.

14:52.024 --> 14:53.787
My mom's record is 12 seconds.

14:53.893 --> 14:55.952
- Neil, I think you're old enough to...
- Go!

14:56.061 --> 14:59.053
- Would you stop kicking? Just hold still.
- That's tickling. It tickles.

14:59.164 --> 15:01.724
- My thumb.
- Hold still. Quit it...

15:04.603 --> 15:07.436
LaDawn, I thought
we could watch a DVD together.

15:07.539 --> 15:09.939
<i>I picked up the first season
of Jiminy Glick.</i>

15:10.042 --> 15:11.976
Imagine being that guy for a day.

15:12.077 --> 15:16.104
Colin Farrell, so I was talking
to my wife, Dixie, the other day...

15:16.215 --> 15:19.013
and she was saying
that you weren't a very good actor.

15:19.118 --> 15:20.608
And I agreed with her.

15:20.719 --> 15:24.120
Now, why, Colin,
why would we both say that?

15:26.992 --> 15:30.223
All right, that's it.
Jeremy must be destroyed.

15:37.703 --> 15:38.761
Mom?

15:40.839 --> 15:41.806
Dad?

15:42.141 --> 15:44.302
Mom? Is anyone there?

15:48.147 --> 15:50.775
Little man? You in here?

16:02.161 --> 16:06.325
I say, I think this is how you change a tire.
But what do I know? I'm just a baby!

16:08.534 --> 16:12.061
Here's your iPod, so you can listen
to The Streaks while you gasp for air.

16:12.171 --> 16:13.229
[Mumbles]

16:13.339 --> 16:14.567
The Strokes. Right.

16:16.675 --> 16:19.439
Boy, this was a better acquisition
than I thought.

16:19.545 --> 16:22.446
We may even be able to put in
some sorghum this year.

16:27.019 --> 16:29.112
So, anyway...

16:29.221 --> 16:30.654
Hey, I made you a mix tape.

16:30.756 --> 16:32.121
I don't have a dual cassette player...

16:32.224 --> 16:34.784
so, you know, I had to hold
the tape recorder up to the radio...

16:34.893 --> 16:36.656
so the quality is kind of sucky...

16:36.762 --> 16:39.629
but, you know,
all the songs describe my feelings.

16:40.799 --> 16:43.199
I'm sorry, Stewie. I'm just upset.

16:43.869 --> 16:45.632
Jeremy stopped calling me.

16:45.738 --> 16:47.672
He what? That blaggard!

16:47.806 --> 16:51.071
Come here,
let me just hold you for a while.

16:53.012 --> 16:56.243
Stewie! No! That is a bad place to touch.

16:56.348 --> 16:58.407
No. No, no, no, no, no, no.

16:58.517 --> 16:59.541
But...

17:00.285 --> 17:02.048
But I... You...

17:02.921 --> 17:04.252
[Bawling]

17:05.424 --> 17:06.550
No more TV.

17:06.658 --> 17:09.957
Well, how about no more job?
You hear that, Miss Fussy Britches?

17:10.062 --> 17:12.030
I shall see you fired, damn you!

17:12.131 --> 17:16.067
I thought we were going to go all the way
and die together like Hitler and Eva Braun.

17:17.936 --> 17:19.927
<i>- We do everything together, ja?
- Ja.</i>

17:20.039 --> 17:21.301
You got your poison?

17:21.407 --> 17:24.035
Okay. One, two, three.

17:25.110 --> 17:27.977
- You didn't do it.
- You didn't do it, either.

17:28.080 --> 17:30.344
Okay, okay.
This time we really have to do it.

17:30.449 --> 17:32.508
- Okay, all right. You ready? Okay, okay.
- Okay.

17:32.618 --> 17:35.143
- One, two.
- One, two.

17:38.791 --> 17:42.318
You want me to kill myself
and you're not going to.

17:42.428 --> 17:45.488
- You suck. You suck.
- You suck.

17:50.202 --> 17:53.433
Hey, Stewie, there's something
thunking around in the trunk of my car...

17:53.539 --> 17:55.700
and I can't get in there
'cause somebody busted the lock.

17:55.808 --> 17:57.469
You have any idea what that's about?

17:57.576 --> 18:00.272
That. It's this whole...

18:00.946 --> 18:03.437
It's this whole crazy thing.

18:07.653 --> 18:09.883
Hey, this is not a barn, young lady.

18:10.155 --> 18:11.850
I'm just so exhausted.

18:12.057 --> 18:14.958
You know, I thought I'd be happy
being with Neil, but I'm not.

18:15.060 --> 18:16.118
This is horrible.

18:16.228 --> 18:19.061
Sweetheart, we'll figure some way
to get you out of this.

18:19.164 --> 18:21.166
Brian, did you find any loophole
in the contract?

18:21.266 --> 18:22.528
Nope, it's airtight.

18:22.634 --> 18:24.761
The only way out
is if Neil commits an infidelity.

18:24.870 --> 18:27.998
Well, that's it then.
We got to find somebody to seduce Neil.

18:28.540 --> 18:30.974
- Who, me?
- Well, if not you, Lois, then who?

18:31.076 --> 18:32.566
Beverly D'Angelo?

18:32.678 --> 18:34.236
'Cause I don't think she'd do it.

18:34.346 --> 18:36.177
And I don't even know
how to get ahold of her.

18:39.551 --> 18:41.018
Hello, LaDawn.

18:41.120 --> 18:44.021
Listen, I certainly hope you'll excuse
last night's indiscretion.

18:44.123 --> 18:47.388
It was just... Oh, my God, LaDawn!
What's that on your neck?

18:54.066 --> 18:56.159
Lois! Thank God you're here, Lois.

18:56.268 --> 19:00.068
It was all her friends.
They were doing marijuana and heroin.

19:00.172 --> 19:02.936
And they were taking eczema
and touching each other.

19:03.041 --> 19:05.373
- LaDawn, wake up this instant.
- What?

19:06.411 --> 19:08.242
- I don't...
- You know what? Don't bother, LaDawn.

19:08.347 --> 19:09.405
You are fired.

19:11.049 --> 19:13.017
Well, I really don't know
how this happened...

19:13.118 --> 19:15.211
but I guess this is the last time
I get to see you.

19:16.555 --> 19:18.386
I'm gonna miss you, little guy.

19:19.258 --> 19:20.691
This is for you.

19:22.261 --> 19:24.126
She made me a mix tape.

19:24.229 --> 19:27.596
Oh, dear God, what have I done?
I've made a terrible mistake.

19:28.167 --> 19:31.227
LaDawn! LaDawn!

19:32.237 --> 19:35.138
LaDawn!

19:36.808 --> 19:37.934
All right, you all set, honey?

19:38.043 --> 19:40.944
LOIS: I can't believe I'm doing this.
It's so disgusting.

19:41.046 --> 19:42.479
But it's for my little girl.

19:42.581 --> 19:44.310
Dad, how do you know Neil will show up?

19:44.416 --> 19:47.783
Don't worry, Meg.
I sent him an invitation he couldn't refuse.

19:53.926 --> 19:57.589
Strange. These conventions
usually have Segway parking.

19:58.630 --> 20:01.155
Hello? Am I too late for the Q&A?

20:01.333 --> 20:05.565
Yeah, but you're just in time for the T&A.

20:06.405 --> 20:08.202
Mrs. Griffin, what are you...

20:09.341 --> 20:11.741
You can call me Mystique.

20:11.843 --> 20:13.674
Mrs. Griffin, this is wrong.

20:13.779 --> 20:16.077
Well, well, well, look at this, Meg.

20:16.181 --> 20:19.275
Your boyfriend is violating
both your contract and my wife.

20:19.384 --> 20:23.946
Meg, I wasn't doing anything.
Mrs. Griffin was just... You're bending it.

20:24.056 --> 20:25.080
I don't care.

20:25.190 --> 20:28.284
You've nullified the contract. I'm free!

20:28.994 --> 20:30.086
Free?

20:30.762 --> 20:33.754
I don't understand, Meg.
You don't want to be my girlfriend?

20:33.865 --> 20:36.800
Well, I thought I did.
But I guess I was just jealous.

20:36.902 --> 20:37.891
I see.

20:38.003 --> 20:41.166
Well, Meg, I want you to be with me
because you want to be with me...

20:41.273 --> 20:43.002
not because you have to.

20:44.009 --> 20:45.374
Thank you, Neil.

20:45.644 --> 20:48.010
Cecilia, it's The Goldman.

20:48.113 --> 20:49.910
How about we fire up the old Segway...

20:50.015 --> 20:52.677
and find a nice quiet field
to do long division in?

20:52.784 --> 20:57.016
I mean, a nice quiet field
in which to do long division. Sorry.

20:57.289 --> 20:58.756
Sorry, everybody.

20:58.857 --> 21:00.085
Okay, I'm on my way.

21:00.192 --> 21:04.151
He's going back to Cecilia?
I can't believe I'm actually jealous.

21:04.263 --> 21:06.254
I can't believe I actually touched him.

21:06.365 --> 21:08.526
I still can't believe it's not butter.

21:09.635 --> 21:11.432
Next week I run for mayor of Quahog.

21:11.536 --> 21:13.902
Do I have what it takes?
We'll find out. Don't miss it.

21:22.781 --> 21:27.480
Well, here we are again.
Another Saturday night with basic cable.

21:28.787 --> 21:29.811
Yep.

21:30.656 --> 21:33.523
I suppose neither of us
is really cut out for love, and we...

21:33.625 --> 21:36.025
Oh, my God! Jeremy's still in the trunk!

21:36.128 --> 21:37.595
Oh, God, how long has it been?

21:37.696 --> 21:40.494
Let's see. Two weeks. Yep.

21:41.266 --> 21:42.563
Yeah, he's dead.

21:43.502 --> 21:44.867
Definitely dead.

21:44.868 --> 22:45.868
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru